    "body": "I tried to inference the model using this https://github.com/Alpha-VLLM/LLaMA2-Accessory/tree/main/SPHINX#single-gpu-inference\r\nresulting in the following error:\r\n`\r\nRuntimeError: expected mat1 and mat2 to have the same dtype, but got: float != c10::Half`\r\n\r\nWould you please share an example to run inference on a single image with a single prompt? \r\n\r\nMy code so far:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom SPHINX import SPHINXModel\r\nfrom PIL import Image\r\n\r\nmodel = SPHINXModel.from_pretrained(pretrained_path=\"GUIAgent-InternLM7B\", with_visual=True)\r\n\r\nimage = Image.open(\"my_image.png\")\r\n\r\nqas = \"Identify all clickable elements on the screen and provide their 2D bounding boxes in the format of [x1,y1,x2,y2].\"\r\n\r\nresponse = model.generate_response([[qas, None]], image, temperature=0)\r\n\r\nprint(response)\r\n```",
